---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CinematicHero from '../components/CinematicHero';
import Highlights from '../components/Highlights';
import LocalNav from '../components/LocalNav.astro';
import ProductUniverse from '../components/ProductUniverse';
import ProjectExplorer from '../components/ProjectExplorer';
import { projects } from '../data/projects';
import type { Project } from '../data/projects';

const highlightSlugs = ['divyadhun', 'civicproof', 'watchroom', 'instafetch', 'resume-fit-checker', 'frost-and-flowers'];
const highlightProjects = highlightSlugs.map((slug) => projects.find((project) => project.slug === slug)).filter((project): project is Project => Boolean(project));
const appProjects = projects.filter((project) => project.filters.includes('android'));
const webProjects = projects.filter((project) => project.filters.includes('websites'));
const aiProjects = projects.filter((project) => project.filters.includes('ai'));
---
<BaseLayout>
  <LocalNav />
  <CinematicHero client:media="(min-width: 621px)" projects={highlightProjects} />

  <section id="highlights" class="highlights-section section-grid" aria-labelledby="highlights-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="editorial-heading reveal-on-scroll"><p class="eyebrow"><span>02</span> First contacts / selected work</p><h2 id="highlights-title">Find the<br /><em>signal.</em></h2><p>Move through six verified builds. Each one is a different answer to the same question: what deserves to exist?</p></div>
      <Highlights client:visible projects={highlightProjects} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="projects" class="universe-section section-grid" aria-labelledby="universe-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="editorial-heading editorial-heading--split reveal-on-scroll"><div><p class="eyebrow"><span>03</span> The Aman archive / constellation</p><h2 id="universe-title">Navigate the<br /><em>build system.</em></h2></div><p>Switch the lens. A node is a project; a line is a documented relationship. Select one to move from distance into evidence.</p></div>
      <ProductUniverse client:visible projects={projects} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="apps" class="discipline-section discipline-section--apps section-grid" aria-labelledby="apps-title">
      <div class="shell discipline-layout"><div class="discipline-copy reveal-on-scroll"><p class="eyebrow"><span>04</span> Domain / Android</p><h2 id="apps-title">Systems you can<br /><em>hold in your hand.</em></h2><p>Offline states, playback ownership, room lifecycle and the decisions people feel in a physical device.</p></div><div class="discipline-list reveal-on-scroll">{appProjects.map((project, index) => <a href={`/projects/${project.slug}/`} class="discipline-row"><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><strong>{project.name}</strong><small>{project.status}</small><i>↗</i></a>)}</div></div>
  </section>

  <section id="web" class="discipline-section discipline-section--web section-grid" aria-labelledby="web-title">
      <div class="shell discipline-layout"><div class="discipline-copy reveal-on-scroll"><p class="eyebrow"><span>05</span> Domain / public web</p><h2 id="web-title">Surfaces that<br /><em>earn attention.</em></h2><p>Public products earn trust through clear states, honest boundaries and the small details between a first click and a useful outcome.</p></div><div class="discipline-list reveal-on-scroll">{webProjects.map((project, index) => <a href={`/projects/${project.slug}/`} class="discipline-row"><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><strong>{project.name}</strong><small>{project.status}</small><i>↗</i></a>)}</div></div>
  </section>

  <section id="ai" class="discipline-section discipline-section--ai section-grid" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
      <div class="shell discipline-layout"><div class="discipline-copy reveal-on-scroll"><p class="eyebrow"><span>06</span> Domain / AI + automation</p><h2 id="ai-title">Less repetition.<br /><em>More agency.</em></h2><p>Automation should explain itself. RecruitOS AI keeps analysis local-first, suggestions reviewable and the user in control of the final edit.</p></div><div class="discipline-list reveal-on-scroll">{aiProjects.map((project, index) => <a href={`/projects/${project.slug}/`} class="discipline-row"><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><strong>{project.name}</strong><small>{project.status}</small><i>↗</i></a>)}</div></div>
  </section>

  <section id="about" class="about-section section-grid" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <div class="shell about-grid"><div class="about-statement reveal-on-scroll"><p class="eyebrow"><span>07</span> Product development / talent acquisition</p><h2 id="about-title">Build useful things.<br /><em>Bring people in.</em></h2></div><div class="about-copy reveal-on-scroll"><p class="large-copy">I build independent Android, web and AI products — and bring 7+ years of technical talent experience across IT, federal and healthcare work.</p><p class="about-context">LinkedIn-listed: Agama Solutions Inc. · Top Performer recognition (2021, 2022, 2024) · Technical Recruitment Certification (2022) · LinkedIn Recruiter Assessment (2025).</p><div class="principles"><div><span>01 / PRODUCTS</span><strong>From brief to working surface.</strong><p>Android apps, public web tools and AI-assisted workflows.</p></div><div><span>02 / PEOPLE</span><strong>Technical talent acquisition.</strong><p>IT, federal and healthcare recruiting experience.</p></div><div><span>03 / PRACTICE</span><strong>Evidence before claims.</strong><p>Clear product status, honest boundaries and traceable work.</p></div></div></div></div>
  </section>

  <section id="comparison" class="archive-section section-grid" aria-labelledby="comparison-title">
    <div class="shell"><div class="editorial-heading editorial-heading--split reveal-on-scroll"><div><p class="eyebrow"><span>08</span> Explore all projects</p><h2 id="comparison-title">The complete<br /><em>build record.</em></h2></div><p>Search the evidence-backed archive by category, stack or status. Public links stay public; private work stays intentionally high-level.</p></div><ProjectExplorer client:visible /><div class="archive-link-row"><a class="arrow-link" href="/projects/">Open the full archive <span>↗</span></a><span>{projects.length.toString().padStart(2, '0')} documented projects</span></div></div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="contact-section section-grid" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
    <div class="shell contact-card reveal-on-scroll"><div><p class="eyebrow"><span>09</span> Your move</p><h2 id="contact-title">Have a good<br /><em>problem?</em></h2></div><div class="contact-card__right"><p>Tell me what you’re trying to make, untangle or bring back to life. I’ll bring curiosity, structure and a bias toward shipping.</p><a class="contact-email" href="mailto:amansharma.i5@gmail.com">amansharma.i5@gmail.com <span>↗</span></a><div class="contact-links"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/amansharmanm/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/amansharma-it5" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a></div></div></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
